'''The Dancing Dervish''' is a [[unique]] {{il|Reaver Sword}}.

==Mechanics==
The Dancing Dervish grants level 15 {{sl|id=ManifestDancingDervishes}}. Manifest Dancing Dervishes will be supported by any applicable [[support gem]]s socketed into The Dancing Dervish; it is not necessary to have the [[socket]]s be linked together. Manifest Dancing Dervishes will spawn upon reaching 15 consecutive [[Rampage]] Kills. The manifested dervishes do not deactivate when swapping to different weapons, however, the weapon slots containing The Dancing Dervish will remain disabled while the Dervishes are active. 

While The Dancing Dervishes are manifested, the player character is considered [[unarmed]] and gains {{stl|Onslaught}}, therefore effects such as {{il|Facebreaker}}'s, {{il|Doryani's Fist}}'s, or [[Hollow Palm Technique]]'s unarmed damage bonus will take effect. As soon as Rampage ends, the manifested weapons will vanish and the character reequips the weapon, re-enabling the weapon slots.  

{{c|mod|Melee Hits count as Rampage Kills}}: This modifier applies only to hits with The Dancing Dervish. It does not apply to the dancing dervish minions.<ref name="Dancing Dervish rework 1a" />

{{il|The Writhing Jar}}, {{il|Vaal Breach}} etc. can be used to sustain Rampage while there are no nearby enemies to kill (or hit), or if the only enemies are invulnerable, such as during certain boss immunity phases. Due to the "Melee Hits count as Rampage Kills" modifier it is possible gain two Rampage Kills per enemy, if you kill the enemy with a melee hit. This includes the worms from {{il|The Writhing Jar}} that are destroyed on hit.

The minions themselves have 95% less damage taken; it is possible for the minions to get damaged, however they are unlikely to die as long as they have even just a small amount of regen or leech.<ref>https://www.reddit.com/r/pathofexile/comments/9or6gs/comment/e7wwwgf/</ref> They can however die from engaging with large packs of enemies in a map with [[damage reflection]], or from being consumed by [[Summon Reaper]]. If one or both dervishes are killed, they cannot be re-summoned until rampage is gained again. These minions are damageable and can be targeted by [[Link skill]]s if the "{{c|mod|Link Skills can target Damageable Minions}}" [[Minion Defence Mastery]] node is allocated. Linked players do not die when these minions die due to Rampage's effect ending, despite the item's wording.

The minions also have a 25% chance to grant the player a Rampage Kill when hitting Rare or Unique enemies.

Dancing dervish minions are considered manifested minions. Some effects refer to manifested minions, such as those granted by {{il|Chains of Command}}. Dancing dervishes are ''not'' considered [[Animate Weapon|animated weapons]].

The T17 Map modifier {{c|mod|Rare and Unique Monsters in Area are Possessed by X to X Tormented Spirits and their Minions are Touched}} found in some [[Valdo's Puzzle Box]] maps causes the Dancing Dervish minions to be [[possessed]] and, depending on the random {{c|torment|Grip}} modifiers it receives, can greatly increase the minions' damage output.

All modifiers on the The Dancing Dervish item itself apply to the minions once manifested, including [[enchantment]]s, [[corrupted implicit modifier]]s, [[Scourge modifier]]s, and [[Crucible passive tree]]s (except modifiers which allocate player [[notable]] [[passive skill]]s, as minions do not have access to your passive tree).

